atlas institutional-relationship-types

architecture institutional-relationship-types
  canonical_name InstitutionalRelationshipTypes
  owns RelationshipKind
  consumes InstitutionEnvelope
  consumes ProviderState
  consumes Authority
  publishes RelationshipKind
  publishes RelationshipClosure
  family institutional
  domain Institution / Relationship ownership
  layer institutional
  semantic_question Who owns this relationship, which realization sits under it, and what does a downstream estate actually receive from it?
  purpose Separate the commercial or institutional relationship from the product, account, organization and resource that realize it, so that owning a relationship, holding a capability, owning a resource and being authorized to act are four distinct facts.
  maturity architectural
  node_types Relationship
  node_types RelationshipOwner
  node_types Realization
  node_types AccountIdentity
  edge_types owns_relationship
  edge_types realized_by
  edge_types grants_closure_to
  invariant a relationship names a counterparty institution, not a product; the product is a realization beneath it
  invariant exactly one estate owns a relationship; other estates receive bounded closures of it
  invariant relationship ownership, capability availability, resource ownership and downstream authority are four separate facts and are never inferred from one another
  invariant an account or organization identity is evidence of a realization, not proof of an agreement
  invariant an agreement is recorded only when its terms are known; an unknown agreement is recorded as unknown rather than assumed
  forbidden_inference a downstream estate using a provider -> that estate owning the relationship
  forbidden_inference an organization identity existing -> a commercial agreement being in place
  forbidden_inference a provider being publicly available -> a specific estate being entitled to it
  forbidden_inference holding a credential -> holding the authority the credential can reach
  interacts institutional-root
  interacts delegation-model
  interacts authority
  source_lineage Generation-10 product topology separation, 2026-08-26

relationship_kind commercial-provider
  detail Counterparty sells a product or service to the owning estate. Realized by accounts, organizations, subscriptions and rails.

relationship_kind accounting-realization
  detail Counterparty holds the owning estate's books of record. Financial Metabolism derives the position; the counterparty realizes the accounting.

relationship_kind institutional
  detail University, publisher, non-profit or civic counterparty. Realized by contacts, programs and eligibility rather than by accounts.

relationship_kind direct-collaboration
  detail A live project relationship with issues, PRs, maintainers and upstream response. Distinct from a Partner Commons method profile covering the same project.

relationship_kind managed-client
  detail The owning estate operates software or service on the counterparty's behalf. The counterparty has its own downstream organizations and users.

relationship_kind prospect
  detail Not yet an agreement. Lives in a demo world with its own effect policy until conversion.
